Z||000000||SloPonti||12-08-1999||12:42 AM||||i have an 84 coupe and i bought the hooker header for the four cylinder! should i wrap the header? i know the best thing to do is to ceramic coat it but i don't have that much money? also if i wrap it should i do it after i run the car for awhile or before i even put it on the car?<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000001||2FAST4U||12-08-1999||02:46 AM||||While header wrap does work as advertized, it is not a good idea for a street car. The header wrap absorbes and holds moisture when driven in the rain, taken to a car wash, ETC. This causes rust, corrosion, and premature failure.<P>I'd suggest running your header as is until you can afford to have it coated.<P>I had my Hooker header coated inside and out by Swain Coatings. It works so well that I can almost keep my hand on the header with the engine running.<P>Swain has a web site and I believe it is SWAINTECH.COM<P>A suggestion - The Hooker header works great but chunk the gasket that came with the header and get a quality gasket from FelPro or Victor<P>||||reg||1
